# Template for .devcontainer/.env — the REAL file is generated by `make env`
# (or .devcontainer/gen-env.sh) with a strong random password and is gitignored.
# This example is committed for documentation only; it holds no real secret.
#
# Both the db sidecar and claude-code load .env via compose `env_file`.

# --- db sidecar (postgres entrypoint) ---
POSTGRES_USER=claude
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=changeme-generated-by-make-env
POSTGRES_DB=claude

# --- Agent Toolkit for AWS (optional; consumed via compose interpolation) ---
# Profile names are specific to YOUR AWS setup, so nothing is shipped by default.
# `gen-env.sh` never rewrites an existing .env, so lines you add here survive.
#
# Space-separated profiles from ~/.claude/aws/config. The FIRST is the MCP
# server's default; the rest are selectable per tool call (`aws_profile`).
# Put the LEAST privileged account first — it is what an unqualified call uses.
#AWS_MCP_PROFILES=sandbox development shared_services management production
#
# Region for the MCP endpoint + the skill catalog (default us-east-1).
#AWS_MCP_REGION=us-east-1
#
# 1 = read-only (describe, don't mutate). Default 0 — the MCP tools can create,
# modify and delete real resources in whichever profile is selected.
#AWS_MCP_READ_ONLY=1

# --- claude-code (libpq client vars + URL) ---
PGHOST=db
PGPORT=5432
PGUSER=claude
PGPASSWORD=changeme-generated-by-make-env
PGDATABASE=claude
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://claude:changeme-generated-by-make-env@db:5432/claude
